## Canonical Sources Of Truth

- `AGENTS.md`
  - short repo map and durable pointers
- `PLANS.md`
  - active, blocked, or recently completed execution registry
- `docs/engineering/project_principles.md`
  - durable cross-cutting rules and doc ownership boundaries
- `docs/codex/TASKS_BACKLOG.md`
  - tracked future work that is not active
- `docs/codex/AGENT_EXECUTION_PITFALLS.md`
  - recurring execution mistakes

## Working Defaults

- For any task that changes repository state, open `PLANS.md` first.
- Use a compact checked queue item for small bounded tasks.
- Use a full active plan with baseline and work-queue checkboxes for multi-step or resumable work.
- Promote active work from `docs/codex/TASKS_BACKLOG.md` into `PLANS.md` before implementation.
- Compact or archive completed plan detail so stale context does not stay in active files.
- Keep `AGENTS.md` short.
- Prefer quiet, targeted validation over broad noisy runs.
